  "summary": "Recent preprints dissect how chaperone-like factors, coactivator assembly, and TFIID sequestration shape transcriptional output.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is how the transcription machinery is assembled and tuned through protein oligomerization, chaperone association, and subunit availability. Small heat shock protein fusion enhances transcription factor potency through oligomerization, raising genomic occupancy and target-gene activation in mammalian cells. Prefoldin associates physically with the histone chaperone FACT and promotes co-transcriptional eviction of macroH2A1 nucleosomes during elongation. In yeast, the SAGA DUB module assembles through sequential co-translational interactions before post-translational docking onto the core. A LisH-derived dimerization motif squelches transcription by sequestering TFIID subunit Taf5, and one peptide slowed growth of human colorectal cancer cells.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
